  "scope": [
    "New stack modes cover zero, one and four elements, both data directions, and invalid counts on an explicitly bounded 32 KiB stack. The maximum 1024-element case runs on the ordinary stack.",
    "Both old-runtime controls fault at stores in the I/O runtime; the same tests pass with the corrected runtime. Guest ELF hashes were checked.",
    "Both heap application sequences and all 22 heap cases pass with the current launcher, including operation-PC and cleanup checks. The unbounded controls reach exit 90.",
    "The snapshot launcher passes all 11 socket cases. The current launcher passes 10; inet-dgram fails at socket-contract.c:198 with EFAULT for both the corrected and unchanged pre-fix images.",
    "The initial full heap attempt on the snapshot launcher stopped in the healthy eventfd test (exit 65), before heap qualification. It is not a passing heap run.",
    "Port recipe flag selection and shell syntax were checked. Full FFmpeg/tshark workloads, concurrency and RTL were not rerun."
